{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlNormalisation","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumerationFintype"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.sum_dim_jonesMarkovCoeff_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.sum_dim_jonesMarkovCoeff_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.lean#L72-L95","doc":"**The unconditional M1 on the List carrier.** For the principal specialisation\n`X = Q^r`, the concrete Jones–Markov weights, summed over the SYT-weighted\ndiagrams of size `n`, normalise to one:\n\n  `∑_{ν : |ν| = n} f^ν · jonesMarkovCoeff Q (Q^r) ν.rowLens = 1`.\n\nTermwise equal (via `jonesMarkovCoeff_rowLens_eq_wenzlWeight`) to the proved\n`QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dim_wenzlWeight_eq_one`; the normalisation is *derived*, not\nassumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.jonesMarkovCoeff_rowLens_eq_wenzlWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.jonesMarkovCoeff_rowLens_eq_wenzlWeight","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.lean#L54-L70","doc":"**Per-diagram carrier identity.** The List-carrier Jones–Markov weight on the\nrow-length list of `ν` is the YoungDiagram-carrier Wenzl weight of `ν`, at the\nprincipal specialisation `X = Q^r`. Numerator by the carrier bridge\n(`schurElement Q (Q^r) ν.rowLens = schurPrincipal r Q ν`), denominator by\n`wenzlNormalisation (|ν|) = [r]_Q^{|ν|}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.levelBracket_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.levelBracket_eq","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.lean#L47-L52","doc":"The Wenzl level bracket `[r]_Q = ∑_{i<r} Q^i` in the `(1−X)/(1−Q)` form used\nby `wenzlNormalisation` at `X = Q^r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.rowLens_sum_eq_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.rowLens_sum_eq_card","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation.lean#L39-L45","doc":"The sum of a diagram's row lengths is its number of cells. Reuses\n`card_cells_ofRowLens` on `μ.rowLens`, which reconstitutes `μ` via\n`ofRowLens_to_rowLens_eq_self`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}